INSERT INTO sdpt_data_trnf.udp_brnz.dq_results_cohort
  (cohort_id, raised_run_id, raised_ts, member_result_ids, member_rule_ids, member_count, affected_tables, total_violation_rows, root_cause_hypothesis, evidence_summary, blast_radius_tables, blast_radius_count, severity, business_domain, owner_group, rank_score, recommended_approach, recommended_approach_type, playbook_id, recommendation_source, model_endpoint, model_input_payload, triage_job_run_id, is_recurrence)
VALUES
  ('f588b56a-c8ba-5d11-9dcf-82bdaf94450b', 'f92379b6-4c04-50a6-ae2f-21b671914173', TIMESTAMP '2026-08-28 03:00:00', array('6b4740de-480a-5c14-86bc-bdd74ab6a8d8', '5e1a2660-adfc-5530-938f-8f86610ac1fd', 'd01b2375-fe94-588e-b797-177ce6ce8189', 'af5705f0-b715-587a-bbbb-9948ba8d5ad1', 'bb6056ac-9992-512b-9cbc-2fac4ef95057', 'e844fe28-517a-5bf6-8836-62da8865d5e2', '415ba943-a726-5843-a83b-1d2bfe903e78', '0d62ff64-dfed-537f-a8ee-e5afb620f1a9', 'ec570042-f1f2-52ed-8bcd-5bbb18f6f133'), array('CTCT_EML_FMT', 'CTCT_EML_NO_AT', 'CTCT_EML_WHITESPACE', 'CTCT_EML_DOMAIN_TLD', 'CTCT_EML_DOUBLE_DOT', 'CTCT_EML_TRAILING_DOT', 'CTCT_EML_NOT_NULL', 'CTCT_EML_STTS_NOT_NULL', 'XREF_OPEN_TS_AGREEMENT'), 9, array('sdpt_data_trnf.udp_brnz.dq_mock_ctct_c', 'sdpt_data_trnf.udp_brnz.dq_mock_subs_c'), 533, 'A change to the CRM contact export on 2026-08-28 broke email serialisation. Nine rules across two tables were clean on every run up to 2026-08-27 and breached together on the first run after. The 240 affected addresses fall into six equal buckets of 40 -- @ replaced by a space, @ dropped entirely, whitespace in the local part, missing top-level domain, doubled dots, trailing dot -- which is the shape of a formatter emitting six variants, not of 240 people mistyping.', 'Zero violations on runs up to 2026-08-27, 240 from 2026-08-28 onward, on all six email rules simultaneously. EML_STTS_CD already flags all 240 as INVALID, so the source\'s own validator agrees the addresses are bad -- meaning the defect is in serialisation, not in validation. XREF_OPEN_TS_AGREEMENT moved on the same date, which places the change in the export rather than in the email field alone.', array('prod.marketing.campaign_audience', 'prod.billing.invoice_contact', 'prod.customer.customer_360', 'prod.servicing.notification_queue'), 4, 'P1_block', 'Customer', 'dq-stewards-customer', 147, 'Raise an upstream ticket against the 2026-08-28 CRM export release. Do not correct the warehouse copy: the source is still emitting the bad format, so a warehouse fix would be overwritten on the next load and would put the warehouse at odds with the system of record.', 'upstream_ticket', 'PB_UPSTREAM_SOURCE_RELEASE', 'playbook', 'dq-cohort-triage', '{"_fixture": "hand-authored, no model invoked", "member_rule_ids": ["CTCT_EML_FMT", "CTCT_EML_NO_AT", "CTCT_EML_WHITESPACE", "CTCT_EML_DOMAIN_TLD", "CTCT_EML_DOUBLE_DOT", "CTCT_EML_TRAILING_DOT", "CTCT_EML_NOT_NULL", "CTCT_EML_STTS_NOT_NULL", "XREF_OPEN_TS_AGREEMENT"], "member_violation_counts": [240, 80, 80, 40, 40, 40, 1, 1, 11]}', '80c4ee4b-f86b-535f-a442-b2258aa37308', FALSE),
  ('b42685aa-7cb6-5d53-8b57-b7e3abba49f1', 'd4d82c3c-a3ee-51b2-a2de-fd2900abeb8f', TIMESTAMP '2026-08-07 03:00:00', array('0dc378de-1853-52d4-97b7-3e94f0ec593e', '74eeb812-a600-5be7-945f-ddae4d7cd372'), array('SUBS_IMEI_NOT_NULL', 'SUBS_PRIM_ACCT_NOT_ZERO'), 2, array('sdpt_data_trnf.udp_brnz.dq_mock_subs_c'), 733, 'Neither of these is a data defect. Both rules were authored without a scope_filter and are firing on rows that legitimately do not carry the column: all 200 IMEI violations are Fixed Broadband services, which have no handset, and all 500 billing- account violations are prepaid services, which have no billing account. The cohort\'s root cause is in the rule registry, not in prod.customer.subs_c.', 'Perfect correlation with product line: 200/200 IMEI violations have PROD_TYPE_KEY = 0 (Fixed Broadband); 500/500 account violations have BILL_SUBS_TYPE_CD = \'PREPAID\'. The correctly-scoped twin rules on the same data return zero -- SUBS_SIM_NOT_NULL scoped to PROD_TYPE_KEY <> 0, and SUBS_BILL_OFFR_NOT_ZERO scoped to POSTPAID. SUBS_MSISDN_FMT already had this defect and was fixed the same way in rule_version 2.', array(), 0, 'P3_monitor', 'Customer', 'dq-stewards-customer', 26, 'Reject the cohort -- the 700 rows are correct. Author rule_version 2 of both rules carrying the scope_filter (PROD_TYPE_KEY <> 0 and BILL_SUBS_TYPE_CD = \'POSTPAID\' respectively) and promote through the registry. The rejection is the audit record that the rows were examined and found correct.', 'accept_and_document', 'PB_RULE_SCOPE_AMENDMENT', 'playbook', 'dq-cohort-triage', '{"_fixture": "hand-authored, no model invoked", "member_rule_ids": ["SUBS_IMEI_NOT_NULL", "SUBS_PRIM_ACCT_NOT_ZERO"], "member_violation_counts": [212, 521]}', '2d64c36b-ccf7-5614-9d21-8b46300f362b', FALSE),
  ('bec13940-d856-5775-9bea-ec68bc38bbae', 'fe30fc6b-1fc6-50b2-977a-fa9404e610ed', TIMESTAMP '2026-08-14 03:00:00', array('fca1aaf9-705f-5724-8202-aa46670b30bb', 'af0a4ba5-3135-5949-b5e5-efcc6bcf3668'), array('SUBS_MSISDN_SENTINEL', 'SUBS_MSISDN_FMT'), 2, array('sdpt_data_trnf.udp_brnz.dq_mock_subs_c'), 23, 'Twelve mobile subscriptions -- ten of them active, two since cancelled -- carry the literal \'service-number-unknown\' in place of an MSISDN. One placeholder repeated twelve times is a provisioning path that completes the subscription record before the resource is issued, not twelve independent data-entry errors.', 'All twelve share the identical literal value and PRIM_RSRC_TYPE_KEY = 1 (mobile); ten carry SUBS_STTS_KEY = 1 and two are cancelled. Both breaching rules resolve to the same twelve rows, so this is one problem seen twice. The uniqueness rule is scoped to exclude the sentinel and therefore passes -- without that scope it would report the same twelve rows a third time.', array('prod.network.service_inventory', 'prod.billing.usage_rating'), 2, 'P1_block', 'Network', 'dq-stewards-network', 116, 'Route to provisioning to issue and publish the twelve resources. Not correctable in the warehouse: the real numbers do not exist in any system yet, so there is nothing to copy.', 'source_correction', 'PB_PROVISIONING_BACKFILL', 'playbook', 'dq-cohort-triage', '{"_fixture": "hand-authored, no model invoked", "member_rule_ids": ["SUBS_MSISDN_SENTINEL", "SUBS_MSISDN_FMT"], "member_violation_counts": [12, 11]}', 'f5a7f720-8532-5158-b9af-eae7332e0a1b', FALSE),
  ('fea104eb-4d4e-5330-9563-d12ce9a0f472', '3877c15d-418c-590a-9e70-06ac511fe278', TIMESTAMP '2026-08-25 03:00:00', array('8f4231f7-3790-5545-9633-802cb3b02985', '32cd3866-a61f-5178-8b40-99d7d168a78f', '712737fe-d793-5138-8c7a-6f9353abb871'), array('CTCT_MOBL_NOT_NULL', 'CTCT_PHN_FMT', 'SUBS_NTWK_NOT_NULL'), 3, array('sdpt_data_trnf.udp_brnz.dq_mock_ctct_c', 'sdpt_data_trnf.udp_brnz.dq_mock_subs_c'), 56, 'Scattered contactability gaps with no shared driver: 18 contacts with no mobile, 24 with a malformed landline, 16 subscriptions with no network technology. Unlike COH-B these do not correlate with any product line -- the 16 network gaps span all three -- so scope is not the explanation. Most likely genuine collection gaps.', 'No product-line correlation and no common load date. CTCT_PHN_FMT is a RECURRENCE: it was verified closed on this rule 13 days ago and breached again 8 days ago at a similar count, which suggests the previous fix corrected rows rather than the process that produces them.', array('prod.servicing.notification_queue'), 1, 'P2_alert', 'Customer', 'dq-stewards-customer', 64, 'Defer pending a field-completion campaign with Customer Operations. Before actioning again, establish why CTCT_PHN_FMT recurred -- re-applying the previous row-level correction will produce the same recurrence in another fortnight.', 'upstream_ticket', 'PB_MANDATORY_FIELD_CAMPAIGN', 'playbook', 'dq-cohort-triage', '{"_fixture": "hand-authored, no model invoked", "member_rule_ids": ["CTCT_MOBL_NOT_NULL", "CTCT_PHN_FMT", "SUBS_NTWK_NOT_NULL"], "member_violation_counts": [16, 24, 16]}', 'f25b9b24-e25f-59ca-937d-d661ecc2f38c', TRUE),
  ('0e970b8e-c656-5035-a747-f8c12481f600', '2bcff611-40f1-5a50-a21c-1f852b56182c', TIMESTAMP '2026-08-20 03:00:00', array('9936ecb0-f8a2-55c8-ac77-b989d6fd1e35', 'dd52e6a6-6c41-50bd-a21e-09791d125bb7'), array('SUBS_ACTV_TS_CONSISTENT', 'XREF_NAME_AGREEMENT'), 2, array('sdpt_data_trnf.udp_brnz.dq_mock_subs_c'), 11, 'Low-volume drift between the subscription and contact records: 10 subscriptions where original and initial activation timestamps disagree, 2 where the subscriber first name does not match the linked contact. Volumes are consistent with legitimate business events -- migrations and name changes -- that the load does not propagate to both tables. No drafted playbook entry matched, so this recommendation is generated.', 'Twelve rows across 1000, stable across every run with no step change. The two name mismatches are both plausible variants rather than corruption.', array('prod.customer.customer_360'), 1, 'P3_monitor', 'Customer', 'dq-stewards-customer', 31, 'GENERATED, not from the playbook. Re-run the load for the affected subscription keys so both tables derive from the same source event. Confirm first that the two name mismatches are not legitimate deed-poll changes, in which case the correct disposition is no_action.', 'pipeline_rerun', NULL, 'generated', 'dq-cohort-triage', '{"_fixture": "hand-authored, no model invoked", "member_rule_ids": ["SUBS_ACTV_TS_CONSISTENT", "XREF_NAME_AGREEMENT"], "member_violation_counts": [10, 1]}', '8460c6ea-e052-5a46-86a9-583c8d0d4b0d', FALSE),
  ('a0e2abd5-7772-581e-bd11-77763a88e195', 'f55ba739-f96f-58e3-8469-7b449147cfae', TIMESTAMP '2026-08-30 03:00:00', array('4149b1c2-5269-5372-a76e-70cc3c5ee265', '64a12d46-8150-5af3-b95f-635f66d12fe9', 'e88537bd-c74b-57a6-aec1-df1f1638d0a2'), array('CTCT_SPCL_CARE_VARIANCE', 'CTCT_BRTH_PARSEABLE', 'CTCT_BRTH_PLAUSIBLE'), 3, array('sdpt_data_trnf.udp_brnz.dq_mock_ctct_c'), 1060, 'Three contact-attribute defects that share a likely cause in how the contact record is defaulted rather than populated. SPCL_CARE_STTS is \'N\' on all 1000 rows -- a vulnerable-customer flag with no variance is almost certainly defaulted, not collected. 14 rows carry the identical literal \'31-02-1988\' as a date of birth, which is both the wrong format and a date that does not exist. 27 contacts are 17 years old.', 'Zero variance on SPCL_CARE_STTS across 1000 rows. All 14 unparseable dates are byte-identical, so this is one bad default value rather than 14 bad records. The 27 minors all have a 2009 birth year.', array('prod.customer.customer_360', 'prod.compliance.vulnerable_customer'), 2, 'P2_alert', 'Customer', 'dq-stewards-customer', 69, 'GENERATED, not from the playbook. Split this cohort: the defaulted special-care flag is a source-capability question for Customer Operations, while the \'31-02-1988\' default is a straightforward source-correction. The 27 minors need a consent and credit-check review before any data change -- do not correct them.', 'source_correction', NULL, 'generated', 'dq-cohort-triage', '{"_fixture": "hand-authored, no model invoked", "member_rule_ids": ["CTCT_SPCL_CARE_VARIANCE", "CTCT_BRTH_PARSEABLE", "CTCT_BRTH_PLAUSIBLE"], "member_violation_counts": [1021, 13, 26]}', '5cd87cb2-1a62-57cc-b6e0-9691ada57fb5', FALSE),
  ('87df1392-93bd-5339-b982-c3b00cd80ffb', '4b75b009-546b-5adb-be3a-74c2b5e3bff9', TIMESTAMP '2026-08-03 03:00:00', array('d8e8782e-376b-5173-be88-78f7a81715f2'), array('SUBS_STTS_RSN_REQUIRED'), 1, array('sdpt_data_trnf.udp_brnz.dq_mock_subs_c'), 20, 'Cancelled subscriptions loaded without a status reason', '22 violations held steady across prior runs, then fell to zero after remediation.', array(), 0, 'P2_alert', 'Customer', 'dq-stewards-customer', 53, 'Cancelled subscriptions loaded without a status reason: correct at source and reload the affected window.', 'pipeline_rerun', 'PB_PIPELINE_RERUN', 'playbook', 'dq-cohort-triage', '{"_fixture": "hand-authored, no model invoked", "member_rule_ids": ["SUBS_STTS_RSN_REQUIRED"], "member_violation_counts": [20]}', '93d716f5-8ecd-5533-b6d0-229667783d9e', FALSE),
